1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,058
Imagine faking 4 million customers to sell your startup to JPMorgan.

2
00:00:04,358 --> 00:00:10,884
The founder of Frank did. Claimed users: 4.25 million. The SEC says fewer than 300,000 were real.

3
00:00:11,234 --> 00:00:15,432
When the bank asked for the list, prosecutors say she had a professor generate fake ones.

4
00:00:15,732 --> 00:00:18,863
JPMorgan paid $175 million.

5
00:00:19,213 --> 00:00:21,755
Guilty on all 4 counts. 85 months.

6
00:00:22,155 --> 00:00:25,271
Real question. How does a bank that big not catch it? Comment.

7
00:00:25,571 --> 00:00:26,994
Follow for the next one.

